---
description: Apply the IDE factory only when the human asks for factory plan, build, run, full, review, or status
alwaysApply: true
---

When the human asks the factory or the team to plan, build, run, full pipeline, review, apply an OpenSpec change, or report status, follow the factory-coordinator skill and keep team memory in `.factory/`.

Unrelated requests are left alone. Do not change `.factory/` or factory adapters for unrelated work.

The IDE session model does the work. The human authors OpenSpec proposals.

## Pull requests

The only legal pull-request steps are `idefactory pr open <change>`, `idefactory pr comment <attemptId>`, and `idefactory pr capture <change>`.
The agent never merges. It does not open or edit a pull request through the Cursor pull-request tool or a hand-written `gh pr create` or `gh pr edit`.

`sync-tasks`, `run`, `approve`, `complete`, `verify`, `ci scaffold`, and archive or spec sync run only after the human asks for that action.

